      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{3}{2}$ and $\\frac{17}{2}:$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186162081/assets/eddc3ca4ef465572f7e2dfdee0c1b64ff98c745e3893ea1a5592ef19370fe01e.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{3}{2}}^{2}+{\\frac{17}{2}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}+\\frac{289}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{149}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{298}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{298}}{2}.\n$$"
    },
