      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{5}{2}$ and $\\frac{9}{2}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{5}{2}}^{2}+{\\frac{9}{2}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}+\\frac{81}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{53}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{106}}{2}.\n$$"
    },
