      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the path $C$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $\\frac{23}{3}$ and $\\frac{11}{4}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =\\sqrt{{\\frac{23}{3}}^{2}+{\\frac{11}{4}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{529}{9}+\\frac{121}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9553}{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{9553}}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{\\sqrt{9553}}{12}.\n$$"
    },
